  "note": "The nouns for figs in Ethiopic and Yemeni Arabic support understanding the Hebrew verb as formed from a fruit name. Whether Amos gathered the fruit or scored it to encourage ripening remains open. The object שִׁקְמִים identifies the trees he tended."
